j8=A.a([A.c(h9,0,"405,080 = four hundred and five thousand (405,000) and eighty (80).","u13_t2_g1",A.a([h9,"four hundred five thousands and eighty","forty-five thousand and eight hundred","four million five thousand and eighty"],j0),"1. How is the number 405,080 written accurately in words?"),A.c(i0,0,'After a number ("five"), we say "five million people", never "five millions people".',"u13_t2_g2",A.a([i0,'Because "people" is a singular noun that requires "There is"','Because "five" must be followed by "of millions"',"Because countries cannot have five million people"],j0),'2. Why is "There are five millions people in that country" grammatically incorrect?'),A.c(i1,0,'Singular "The moon" takes "doesn\'t + base verb (produce)" and affirmative third-person "-s (reflects)".',"u13_t2_g3",A.a([i1,"don't / reflect","isn't / reflecting","doesn't / reflect"],j0),'3. Complete the scientific fact: "The moon _______ produce its own light; it _______ light from the sun."'),A.c("has / share",0,'"Each province" is singular ("has"), while "all 25 provinces" is plural ("share").',"u13_t2_g4",A.a(["has / share","have / shares","has / shares","having / sharing"],j0),"4. Each province in Cambodia _______ its own capital town, and all 25 provinces _______ unique traditions."),A.c(i2,0,'Singular subject "the Mekong River" uses auxiliary "does" + base verb "flow".',"u13_t2_g5",A.a([i2,"How many countries do the Mekong River flows through?","How many countries is the Mekong River flow through?","How many countries does the Mekong River flowing through?"],j0),"5. Which question is grammatically correct in the Present Simple for asking about a geographical fact?"),A.c(i3,0,"8,940 (4 digits) < 89,400 (5 digits) < 809,040 (6 digits) < 8,009,400 (7 digits).","u13_t2_g6",A.a([i3,"8,940 -> 809,040 -> 89,400 -> 8,009,400","8,009,400 -> 809,040 -> 89,400 -> 8,940","89,400 -> 8,940 -> 809,040 -> 8,009,400"],j0),"6. Arrange these four numbers from SMALLEST to BIGGEST: 89,400 \u2022 809,040 \u2022 8,940 \u2022 8,009,400"),A.c("is / live",0,'Singular "surface" takes "is", and plural "marine animals" takes base verb "live".',"u13_t2_g7",A.a(["is / live","are / lives","be / living","was / lived"],j0),'7. Complete the fact: "Almost three quarters of the Earth\'s surface _______ covered by water, and most marine animals _______ in salty oceans."'),A.c(i4,1,'Plural "Polar bears" requires "do not live", not "does not live".',"u13_t2_g8",A.a(["Bamboo grows very quickly in warm wet seasons.",i4,"The sun rises in the east and sets in the west.","Clouds consist of tiny drops of water or ice."],j0),"8. Spot the sentence with a Present Simple grammar mistake:"),A.c("2,050,307",0,"two million (2,000,000) + fifty thousand (50,000) + three hundred and seven (307) = 2,050,307.","u13_t2_g9",A.a(["2,050,307","2,500,307","2,050,370","20,050,307"],j0),'9. Which digits match "two million fifty thousand three hundred and seven"?'),A.c(i5,0,"Country names (like Laos, the Philippines, the United States) are treated as singular subjects.","u13_t2_g10",A.a([i5,"Because plural nouns always take -s verbs in English",'Because "has" and "consists" are past simple verbs',"Because islands and states are uncountable nouns"],j0),'10. Why does "The United States has 50 states, and the Philippines consists of thousands of islands" use singular verbs ("has", "consists")?')],j7)
j7=A.a([A.c(h8,0,"A constitutional monarchy has a monarch as head of state and an elected government.","u13_t2_v1",A.a(["monarchy","province","glacier","volcano"],j0),"1. In a constitutional _______, a King or Queen serves as head of state while an elected Prime Minister leads the government."),A.c(i6,0,"Seasonal monsoon rainfall causes freshwater lakes and rivers to expand in the wet season and shrink in the dry season.","u13_t2_v2",A.a([i6,"It turns into salty ocean water in October","It freezes into solid glaciers during the dry season","It stays the exact same size every single day"],j0),"2. When a country has a wet season and a dry season, how does a large freshwater lake usually change between April and October?"),A.c(i7,0,"Oceans hold salty water; only a small fraction of Earth's water is fresh, and much of that is trapped in glaciers.","u13_t2_v3",A.a([i7,"Because seawater contains 95% oxygen gas","Because rivers only flow inside deep volcanoes","Because fresh water only exists on distant stars"],j0),"3. Even though most of the Earth's surface is covered by water, why can't humans drink seawater directly?"),A.c(d4,0,"Glaciers are thick masses of ice that store most of the planet's fresh water.","u13_t2_v4",A.a(["glaciers","oceans","earthquakes","kilometres"],j0),"4. Huge, slow-moving rivers of ice in cold mountains and polar regions are called _______."),A.c(i8,0,"5 \xd7 4,000 Khmer riels = 20,000 Khmer riels.","u13_t2_v5",A.a([i8,"about 2,000 Khmer riels","about 9,000 Khmer riels","about 200,000 Khmer riels"],j0),"5. If a tourist buys a train ticket for 5 US dollars (when 1 dollar \u2248 4,000 riels), about how many Khmer riels does it cost?"),A.c("volcano",0,"A volcano erupts lava, gas, and ash from beneath the Earth's surface.","u13_t2_v6",A.a(["volcano","glacier","pagoda","province"],j0),"6. A mountain that has an opening at the top from which hot melted rock and ash can erupt is a _______."),A.c(d1,0,"1 kilometre = 1,000 metres.","u13_t2_v7",A.a(["kilometre","percent","degree Celsius","currency"],j0),"7. Which unit of distance is equal to 1,000 metres and is used to measure the distance between cities or provinces?"),A.c("percent",0,'"Percent" (%) means out of 100.',"u13_t2_v8",A.a(["percent","thousand","million","area"],j0),'8. When we say "75 _______ of the students walk to school", which word means "out of every hundred"?'),A.c(i9,0,"The sun is a star, and it looks huge and steady because it is the closest star to Earth.","u13_t2_v9",A.a([i9,"Because the sun is made of cold ocean water","Because distant stars are smaller than mountains","Because the sun only shines during the wet season"],j0),"9. Why does a distant star twinkle at night while our own star, the sun, appears huge and bright in the daytime?"),A.c("representatives",0,"Representatives are elected members of a national assembly.","u13_t2_v10",A.a(["representatives","glaciers","volcanoes","earthquakes"],j0),"10. Elected people who speak and vote for citizens inside a national assembly or parliament are called _______.")],j7)
