h2=A.a([A.c(b3,0,'Steaming hot tea is strong evidence that someone is nearby -> "must".',"g_25_2_1",A.a(["must","can't","might not","mustn't"],g4),"1. The teacup on the table is still steaming hot. Someone _______ be in the kitchen right now."),A.c(b7,1,'To say we are 100% sure something is impossible now, we use "can\'t" (not "mustn\'t").',"g_25_2_2",A.a(["must","can't","could","may"],g4),"2. Sophea just ate two large bowls of noodles ten minutes ago, so she _______ be hungry already!"),A.c(b5,2,'"not sure" + possible owner -> "might belong".',"g_25_2_3",A.a(["must","can't","might","mustn't"],g4),'3. "I\'m not sure whose jacket this is. It _______ belong to Vanna, or maybe Rith."'),A.c(g1,3,'Modal verbs are followed directly by the bare infinitive ("show").',"g_25_2_4",A.a(["The old map could to show a secret cave.","The old map might shows a secret cave.","The old map must showing a secret cave.",g1],g4),"4. Which sentence uses a modal of probability with the correct verb form?"),A.c(b6,0,'"might not have" expresses a negative possibility when we are not certain.',"g_25_2_5",A.a(["might not","must","can","couldn't to"],g4),'5. "Borey hasn\'t replied to my message yet. He _______ have his phone with him during class."'),A.c(g2,1,'We use "can" for general truths ("Mountain weather can change..."), and "could/might/may" for specific present guesses.',"g_25_2_6",A.a(["Where is Dara? He can be in the library right now.",g2,"That strange shadow in the photo mustn't be a bird.","They might to arrive on the evening train."],g4),"6. Contrast general possibility vs specific deduction: Which sentence is grammatically natural?"),A.c(b7,2,'The closed sign makes it impossible -> "can\'t".',"g_25_2_7",A.a(["must","may","can't","might"],g4),'7. The bakery shutters are down and the sign says "CLOSED". You _______ buy bread there tonight.'),A.c(b3,3,'Strong habit + clear evidence -> "It must be Lina."',"g_25_2_8",A.a(["can't","might not","mustn't","must"],g4),'8. "Listen! Someone is playing the violin beautifully upstairs." \u2014 "It _______ be Lina; she practises every evening at seven."'),A.c(b4,0,'"could be poisonous" warns of a real possibility.',"g_25_2_9",A.a(["could","can't","mustn't to","may not to"],g4),'9. "Don\'t touch that strange red berry in the forest \u2014 it _______ be poisonous."'),A.c(g3,1,'Uses "may" and "might" accurately to suggest possible explanations.',"g_25_2_10",A.a(["It mustn't hit a rock in the fog.",g3,"It can't be in the sea.","It must to be a ghost ship."],g4),'10. "The ship disappeared in thick fog, and nobody knows why." Which deduction fits best?')],h1)
