t2=A.a([A.c(k0,0,'Past simple positive ("joined") takes "didn\'t she?"; present perfect negative ("hasn\'t missed") takes "has she?".',"g_32_2_1",A.a([k0,"doesn't she? / hasn't she?","wasn't she? / did she?","did she? / is she?"],s4),'1. Complete the tag questions: "Nary joined the running club last month, _____? And she hasn\'t missed a single training session, _____?"'),A.c("make / do",1,'We say "make a decision" and "do your best".',"g_32_2_2",A.a(["do / make","make / do","make / make","do / do"],s4),'2. Complete the sentence with the right "do" or "make" forms: "Before you _____ a final decision, please _____ your best to check all the data."'),A.c(k1,2,'Present simple habit ("before every flight") + plural subject ("The aircraft engines") -> "are checked".',"g_32_2_3",A.a(["The aircraft engines were checked by technicians before every flight.","The aircraft engines is checked by technicians before every flight.",k1,"Technicians are checked by the aircraft engines before every flight."],s4),'3. Choose the correct passive rewrite: "Technicians check the aircraft engines before every flight."'),A.c(k2,3,'Past simple ("in 2022") + plural object ("These solar gliders") -> "were designed".',"g_32_2_4",A.a(["These solar gliders are designed by two young engineers in 2022.","These solar gliders was designed by two young engineers in 2022.","Two young engineers were designed by these solar gliders in 2022.",k2],s4),'4. Choose the correct passive rewrite: "Two young engineers designed these solar gliders in 2022."'),A.c("who",0,'In a non-defining relative clause (after a comma) referring to a person, we must use "who" (never "that").',"g_32_2_5",A.a(["who","which","where","that"],s4),'5. Complete the non-defining relative clause: "Mr. Vannak, _____ used to be a professional sprinter, now coaches our school athletics team."'),A.c("where",1,'"where" introduces a relative clause describing the place where an action happens.',"g_32_2_6",A.a(["who","where","which","when"],s4),'6. Complete the sentence: "The sports centre _____ we do our weight training on Saturdays has brand-new equipment."'),A.c(k3,2,'Ongoing background action ("was testing") interrupted by a sudden short event ("went off").',"g_32_2_7",A.a(["tested / was going","was testing / was going",k3,"is testing / went"],s4),'7. Choose the correct past verb forms: "While the programmer _____ the new app, the electricity suddenly _____ off."'),A.c(k4,3,"Person who invents = inventor (+ -or); noun for the process of educating = education (drop -e + -ion).","g_32_2_8",A.a(["The inventer gave a talk about science educater.","The invention gave a talk about science educator.","The inventor gave a talk about science educationship.",k4],s4),'8. Using the Unit 32 suffix rules (-er, -or, -ion), which sentence uses the correct noun forms of "invent" and "educate"?'),A.c(k5,0,"Two simultaneous ongoing past actions use Past Continuous + while + Past Continuous.","g_32_2_9",A.a([k5,"Sophea stretched her legs while her brother jogs around the track.","Sophea was stretching her legs when her brother was jogged.","Sophea stretches her legs while her brother was jogging."],s4),"9. Which sentence correctly describes two actions happening at the exact same time in the past?"),A.c("are they?",1,'"Those sugary energy drinks" is plural and the verb "aren\'t" is negative -> positive tag "are they?".',"g_32_2_10",A.a(["isn't it?","are they?","aren't they?","do they?"],s4),'10. Complete the tag question: "Those sugary energy drinks aren\'t very good for your heart, _____?"')],t1)
o=A.a([A.c(c1,2,"Carbohydrates provide the body and brain with energy.","v_32_2_1",A.a(["infections","programmers","carbohydrates","laboratories"],s4),'1. Complete the sentence: "Runners eat rice, pasta, or bananas before a long race because _____ give their bodies quick energy."'),A.c(c2,3,"Proteins repair body tissue and build muscle.","v_32_2_2",A.a(["emojis","gliders","investigations","proteins"],s4),'2. Complete the sentence: "Fish, eggs, beans, and chicken are rich in _____, which help repair and build strong muscles after exercise."'),A.c("cardio",0,"Cardio exercise raises your heart rate and improves overall fitness.","v_32_2_3",A.a(["cardio","ironing","gardening","painting"],s4),'3. Complete the sentence: "Doing 30 minutes of _____ such as brisk cycling, swimming, or jogging strengthens your heart and lungs."'),A.c(c3,1,"Weight training uses weights or resistance to build muscle strength.","v_32_2_4",A.a(["shopping","weight training","infection","direction"],s4),'4. Complete the sentence: "If you want stronger arms and shoulders, the gym coach recommends safe _____ twice a week."'),A.c(c4,2,'"Unhealthy" means harmful to your physical or mental health.',"v_32_2_5",A.a(["impressed","creative","unhealthy","original"],s4),'5. Complete the sentence: "Staying up until 2 a.m. every night and eating only fried snacks is a very _____ lifestyle."'),A.c(c5,3,"A programmer writes software programs for computers or phones.","v_32_2_6",A.a(["explorer","painter","glider","programmer"],s4),'6. Complete the sentence: "My older cousin works as a computer _____ who writes code for mobile banking apps."'),A.c("glider",0,"A glider is a light winged aircraft that flies without an engine.","v_32_2_7",A.a(["glider","laboratory","protein","promise"],s4),'7. Complete the sentence: "Unlike a modern jet plane, a _____ has no engine and floats on rising currents of air."'),A.c(c7,1,"An explorer travels to unfamiliar places to learn about them.","v_32_2_8",A.a(["producer","explorer","programmer","infection"],s4),'8. Complete the sentence: "Roald Amundsen was a brave polar _____ who led the first expedition to reach the South Pole."'),A.c("data",2,"Data is factual information or measurements collected during an experiment or test.","v_32_2_9",A.a(["juice","sweets","data","dishes"],s4),'9. Complete the sentence: "During the test flight, the pilots recorded wind speed and wing _____ to see how well the plane performed."'),A.c(c8,3,"A film director leads the making of a movie and guides the actors and crew.","v_32_2_10",A.a(["inventor","explorer","painter","director"],s4),"10. Complete the sentence: \"The film _____ shouted 'Action!' and told the camera crew to follow the actors across the bridge.\"")],t1)
o=A.c7("3222","Extension test for Unit 32: Tag questions across tenses, do/make collocations, present/past passive, -or/-er/-ion suffixes, relative clauses, and past simple vs past continuous in fresh contexts.",15,t2,"test_unit_32_2",A.a([A.d("p_32_2_1",A.a([b9],s4),"3 syllables: VI-ta-min","vitamin"),A.d("p_32_2_2",A.a([b9],s4),"3 syllables: e-QUIP-ment","equipment"),A.d("p_32_2_3",A.a([c6],s4),"3 syllables: trans-LA-tor","translator"),A.d("p_32_2_4",A.a([b9],s4),"4 syllables: en-er-GET-ic","energetic"),A.d("p_32_2_5",A.a([f],s4),"4 syllables: tech-NOL-o-gy","technology")],s6),"Unit 32 \u2014 Test 2",g,b0,o)
t2=A.a([A.c(k6,0,'TG p.179 Act 1A #8: "What did you eat for lunch yesterday?"',"g_33_1_1",A.a([k6,"What do you eat for lunch yesterday?","What were you eat for lunch yesterday?","What are you eating yesterday?"],s4),'1. Form the question from Activity 1A #8: "what / eat / lunch / yesterday?"'),A.c(k7,1,'TG p.179 Act 1A #10: "What do you like to do in your free time?"',"g_33_1_2",A.a(["What did you liked to do in free time?",k7,"What are you like do in free time?","What does you like in free time?"],s4),'2. Form the question from Activity 1A #10: "what / like / do / free time?"'),A.c(k8,2,'TG p.180 Act 2 #1: "You mustn\'t talk on your mobile phone in class."',"g_33_1_3",A.a(["You mustn't wear your uniform at school.","You must chew gum in class.",k8,"You must cheat in exams."],s4),'3. Which school rule correctly uses "must" or "mustn\'t" in Activity 2?'),A.c(k9,3,'TG p.180 Act 3 #2: "You should go shopping / go to the market."',"g_33_1_4",A.a(["You mustn't eat dinner.","You can't go to the market.","You went to the market yesterday.",k9],s4),'4. Give advice using "should" for Activity 3 #2: "We don\'t have any food in the house for dinner tonight."'),A.c("a request (R)",0,"TG p.180 Act 4 #4: R (request).","g_33_1_5",A.a(["a request (R)","ability (A)","permission (P)","a warning"],s4),'5. In Activity 4, what does "Can you take me to the bus station on your scooter?" express?'),A.c("permission (P)",1,"TG p.180 Act 4 #5: P (permission).","g_33_1_6",A.a(["ability (A)","permission (P)","a request (R)","past time"],s4),"6. In Activity 4, what does \"At Lynn's cousin's school, you can choose what you want to do in class!\" express?"),A.c(l0,2,'SB p.181 Act 5B: "Does it...?" -> "No, it doesn\'t." / "Is it...?" -> "Yes, it is."',"g_33_1_7",A.a(["it isn't / it does","it can't / it doesn't",l0,"doesn't it / is it"],s4),'7. Complete the short answers in Activity 5B: "Does it live in the river?" \u2014 "No, _____." / "Is it fluffy?" \u2014 "Yes, _____."'),A.c(l1,3,"TG p.182 Act 7 #7: Situation = frightening / worrying; feeling = frightened / worried.","g_33_1_8",A.a(["That's frightened! I'm frightening.","That's worried! I'm worrying.","That's encouraged! I'm encouraging.",l1],s4),'8. Choose the correct -ing / -ed response to "First ever earthquake in Kampung Cham." (Act 7 #7)'),A.c(l2,0,'TG p.182 Act 8 #3: "The farmer said that the droughts always killed the food in his fields."',"g_33_1_9",A.a([l2,"The farmer said that the droughts always kill the food in my fields.","The farmer said that the droughts killing the food in his fields.","The farmer said that the droughts will killed the food."],s4),'9. Report the Farmer\'s sentence (Act 8 #3): "The droughts always kill the food in our fields."'),A.c(l3,1,"TG p.182 Act 8 #6: are -> were; don't hurt -> didn't hurt.","g_33_1_10",A.a(["The radio presenter said that people are scared of insects and don't hurt them.",l3,"The radio presenter said that people were scared of insects but most of them don't hurt us.","The radio presenter said that insects were scared of people."],s4),"10. Report the Radio Presenter's sentence (Act 8 #6): \"People are scared of insects but most of them don't hurt us.\"")],t1)
n=A.a([A.c(l4,2,'TG p.180 Act 2 #4: "You must put your hand up if you want to talk."',"v_33_1_1",A.a(["You mustn't fight with the other students.","You mustn't wear jewellery in class.",l4,"You must wear a crash helmet."],s4),"1. In Activity 2 (School Rules), Picture 4 shows a student raising her hand. What is the rule?"),A.c(l5,3,"TG p.180 Act 2: #3 You mustn't wear a cap in class; #5 You mustn't wear jewellery in class.","v_33_1_2",A.a(["your uniform (#2) and shoes","a crash helmet (#8) and glasses","a backpack and notebook",l5],s4),"2. In Activity 2, what must you NOT wear in class according to Picture 3 and Picture 5?"),A.c(l6,0,"TG p.180 Act 5A: alligator, scorpion, hippopotamus.","v_33_1_3",A.a([l6,"crocodile, beetle, rhinoceros","alligator, snake, polar bear","gecko, mosquito, panda"],s4),'3. Unscramble these three Activity 5A animal names: "igaatllor", "roosncpi", "ppsiuoomtaph".'),A.c(l7,1,"TG p.180 Act 5A: cheetah, hamster, cockroach, mosquito.","v_33_1_4",A.a(["chicken, rabbit, cricket, moth",l7,"cheetah, turtle, gecko, toad","camel, hamster, beetle, butterfly"],s4),'4. Unscramble these four Activity 5A animal names: "ehachte", "sraetmh", "ahcoocckr", "iqtouosm".'),A.c(l8,2,'TG p.181 Act 6: "First, the adult frog produces a lot of eggs stuck together, called frogspawn."',"v_33_1_5",A.a(["a baby frog with legs","the resting stage of a butterfly",l8,"a young beetle larva"],s4),'5. In Activity 6 (Life Cycles), what is "frogspawn"?'),A.c("froglet",3,"TG p.181 Act 6: tadpole with legs -> baby frog called a froglet -> adult frog.","v_33_1_6",A.a(["frogspawn","larva","pupa","froglet"],s4),'6. In the frog life cycle, what stage comes right between "tadpole with legs" and "adult frog"?'),A.c(l9,0,"TG p.181 Act 6: Beetle: eggs -> larva -> pupa -> adult beetle.","v_33_1_7",A.a([l9,"eggs -> caterpillar -> froglet -> adult beetle","frogspawn -> tadpole -> pupa -> adult beetle","pupa -> larva -> eggs -> adult beetle"],s4),"7. In the beetle life cycle, what is the correct 4-stage sequence?"),A.c(m0,1,"SB p.182 Act 6B box: first, then, next, after that, finally.","v_33_1_8",A.a(["before, while, during, until, since",m0,"always, never, sometimes, often, usually","who, which, that, where, when"],s4),"8. Which five sequencers are listed in the Activity 6B box?"),A.c(m1,2,"TG p.182 Act 7 #8: \"That's embarrassing / depressing / frustrating / I'm embarrassed / depressed / worried.\"","v_33_1_9",A.a(["encouraged / inspired","pleased / fascinated",m1,"exhausted / proud"],s4),'9. In Activity 7, which adjective describes how you feel if "Only 5% of rubbish gets recycled in Cambodia"?'),A.c("earthquake",3,'TG p.182 Extension: "It\'s a natural disaster and the ground shakes (earthquake)."',"v_33_1_10",A.a(["hippopotamus","drought","flood","earthquake"],s4),'10. Which word from the TG Extension ("Describe the Word") means "a natural disaster and the ground shakes"?')],t1)
n=A.c7("3321","Covers Unit 33 (Book Pages 179\u2013182): Question prompts, school rules, should advice, can/can't functions, animals, life cycles, -ing/-ed adjectives, and reported speech.",15,t2,"test_unit_33_1",A.a([A.d("p_33_1_1",A.a([c9],s4),"5 syllables: hip-po-POT-a-mus",d0),A.d("p_33_1_2",A.a([c9],s4),"4 syllables: CAT-er-pil-lar",d3),A.d("p_33_1_3",A.a([c9],s4),"2 syllables: COCK-roach",d2),A.d("p_33_1_4",A.a([d4],s4),"3 syllables: mos-QUI-to",m2),A.d("p_33_1_5",A.a([d],s4),"4 syllables: FAS-ci-na-ting",d9)],s6),"Unit 33 \u2014 Test 1",e,b0,n)
t2=A.a([A.c("must / should",0,'"must" expresses a legal rule/obligation; "should" gives good safety advice.',"g_33_2_1",A.a(["must / should","mustn't / shouldn't","can't / mustn't","shouldn't / can"],s4),'1. Choose the correct pair of modals: "Motorbike riders _____ wear a helmet by law, and they _____ check their brakes before a long trip."'),A.c(m3,1,'"Can you ... please?" asks someone to do something for you (a request).',"g_33_2_2",A.a(["Adult frogs can breathe through their skin and lungs.",m3,"Students can use the school library until 4:30 p.m.","My little sister can count to one hundred in English."],s4),'2. In which sentence does "can" express a polite REQUEST rather than ability or permission?'),A.c(m4,2,'In reported speech, present simple verbs ("turns", "becomes") shift back to past simple ("turned", "became").',"g_33_2_3",A.a(["The science teacher said that a caterpillar turn into a pupa before it become a butterfly.","The science teacher said that a caterpillar was turning into a pupa yesterday.",m4,"The science teacher told that a caterpillar turned into a pupa."],s4),'3. Report the science teacher\'s statement: "A caterpillar turns into a pupa before it becomes a butterfly."'),A.c(m5,3,'"I am reading" -> "she was reading", and "I can\'t" -> "she couldn\'t".',"g_33_2_4",A.a(["Lina said that she is reading an article and can't stop smiling.","Lina said that I was reading an article and couldn't stop smiling.","Lina told that she was reading an article and didn't stop smiling.",m5],s4),"4. Report Lina's words: \"I am reading an article about river dolphins, and I can't stop smiling.\""),A.c(m6,0,'The situation was "frustrating" (-ing); the players felt "frustrated" (-ed).',"g_33_2_5",A.a([m6,"frustrated / frustrating","frustrate / frustrating","frustrating / encouraging"],s4),'5. Choose the correct -ing / -ed adjectives: "It was _____ when our team lost the ball five times, so the players looked very _____."'),A.c(m7,1,'Past simple Wh-questions use "Where + did + subject + base verb (go)?".',"g_33_2_6",A.a(["Where did you went with your cousins last Sunday?",m7,"Where were you go with your cousins last Sunday?","Where do you went with your cousins last Sunday?"],s4),"6. Choose the grammatically correct past simple interview question:"),A.c(m8,2,'"Can scorpions...?" -> "Yes, they can." / "Do they...?" -> "No, they don\'t."',"g_33_2_7",A.a(["they do / they can't","it can / it doesn't",m8,"they are / they aren't"],s4),'7. Complete the short-answer dialogue: "Can scorpions survive in dry deserts?" \u2014 "Yes, _____." / "Do they lay frogspawn?" \u2014 "No, _____."'),A.c(m9,3,'"First" starts the process, "Next" (or "Then") continues it, and "Finally" marks the last step.',"g_33_2_8",A.a(["Finally / First / Then","After that / Finally / First","Next / First / Finally",m9],s4),'8. Which sequence of linkers best completes this process: "_____, wash the plastic bottles. _____, remove the old labels. _____, place them in the recycling bin."'),A.c(n0,0,'"don\'t feed" -> "didn\'t feed" and "makes" -> "made".',"g_33_2_9",A.a([n0,"The park ranger said that visitors don't fed the wild monkeys.","The park ranger said that visitors weren't feed the wild monkeys.","The park ranger told that visitors didn't fed the wild monkeys."],s4),"9. Report the park ranger's warning: \"Visitors don't feed the wild monkeys because human food makes them sick.\""),A.c(n1,1,'"should" and "shouldn\'t" give helpful advice for someone who feels ill.',"g_33_2_10",A.a(["You mustn't drink any water today.",n1,"You can play football in the rain this afternoon.","You should eat lots of ice and stay up late."],s4),'10. Choose the best advice for a classmate who says: "I have a sore throat and a high fever today."')],t1)
m=A.a([A.c("uniform",2,"A school uniform is the standard clothing students wear at school.","v_33_2_1",A.a(["crash helmet","jewellery","uniform","caterpillar"],s4),'1. Complete the sentence: "Every morning at Bakan High School, students wear a neat white shirt and blue skirt or trousers as their school _____."'),A.c(d5,3,"A crash helmet protects a rider's head in case of an accident.","v_33_2_2",A.a(["frogspawn","uniform","jewellery","crash helmet"],s4),'2. Complete the sentence: "Always fasten your _____ before riding a scooter or motorbike so your head is protected."'),A.c(d6,0,"Rings, necklaces, and bracelets are examples of jewellery.","v_33_2_3",A.a(["jewellery","tadpoles","headlines","droughts"],s4),'3. Complete the sentence: "For safety during physical education class, students must remove rings, gold chains, and other _____."'),A.c("tadpole",1,"A tadpole hatches from frogspawn and swims in water before growing legs.","v_33_2_4",A.a(["pupa","tadpole","caterpillar","cockroach"],s4),'4. Complete the sentence: "In the pond, a young _____ swims with a long tail before it grows legs and becomes a froglet."'),A.c("pupa",2,"The pupa is the resting transformation stage between larva/caterpillar and adult insect.","v_33_2_5",A.a(["froglet","frogspawn","pupa","scorpion"],s4),'5. Complete the sentence: "Inside a hard shell called a _____, a caterpillar slowly changes into an adult butterfly."'),A.c(d1,3,"A scorpion has pincers and a venomous sting at the end of its curved tail.","v_33_2_6",A.a(["hamster","hippopotamus","tadpole","scorpion"],s4),'6. Complete the sentence: "Be careful when lifting dry rocks in the desert because a _____ can sting you with its curved tail."'),A.c(d8,0,'"Encouraging" (-ing) describes positive news that gives people hope and confidence.',"v_33_2_7",A.a(["encouraging","frightened","worried","embarrassed"],s4),'7. Complete the sentence: "Seeing hundreds of volunteers plant young trees along the river was very _____ news for our town."'),A.c(d7,1,'"Frightened" (-ed) describes how a person feels when they are scared.',"v_33_2_8",A.a(["frightening","frightened","fascinating","encouraging"],s4),'8. Complete the sentence: "The little boy felt _____ when he heard loud thunder outside his bedroom window at midnight."'),A.c("drought",2,"A drought is a long period with little or no rain.","v_33_2_9",A.a(["tsunami","flood","drought","tornado"],s4),'9. Complete the sentence: "When there is no rain for many months, a severe _____ dries up the soil and damages farm crops."'),A.c(m2,3,"A mosquito is a small flying insect that bites people and animals.","v_33_2_10",A.a(["alligator","hippopotamus","hamster","mosquito"],s4),'10. Complete the sentence: "Sleeping under a net at night protects you from being bitten by a _____."')],t1)
m=A.c7("3322","Extension test for Unit 33: Modals (must/mustn't, should/shouldn't, can/can't), sequencers, -ing/-ed adjectives, reported speech backshift, and Unit 33 vocabulary in fresh contexts.",15,t2,"test_unit_33_2",A.a([A.d("p_33_2_1",A.a([d4],s4),"4 syllables: en-VI-ron-ment","environment"),A.d("p_33_2_2",A.a([d],s4),"4 syllables: con-ser-VA-tion","conservation"),A.d("p_33_2_3",A.a([d4],s4),"4 syllables: em-BAR-ras-sing","embarrassing"),A.d("p_33_2_4",A.a([d4],s4),"4 syllables: dis-ap-POINT-ed","disappointed"),A.d("p_33_2_5",A.a([c9],s4),"2 syllables: REP-tile","reptile")],s6),"Unit 33 \u2014 Test 2",e,b0,m)
t2=A.a([A.c(n2,0,'TG p.183 Act 2 #4: "which / that" refers to the book.',"g_34_1_1",A.a([n2,"I just finished reading the book about ghosts who my friend gave me.","I just finished reading the book about ghosts where my friend gave me.","I just finished reading the book about ghosts when my friend gave me."],s4),'1. Combine Activity 2 #4: "I just finished reading the book about ghosts. My friend gave me the book."'),A.c(n3,1,'TG p.183 Act 2 #5: Uses "which / that" for "the inventions".',"g_34_1_2",A.a(["Jana wasn't interested in the inventions who they were talking about.",n3,"Jana wasn't interested in the inventions where they were talking about.","Jana wasn't interested in the inventions when they were talking."],s4),'2. Combine Activity 2 #5: "Jana wasn\'t interested in the inventions. They were talking about them."'),A.c(n4,2,"TG p.184 Act 4: #4 a. has she?; #6 b. wasn't he?.","g_34_1_3",A.a(["hasn't she? / was he?","is she? / didn't he?",n4,"does she? / isn't he?"],s4),'3. Match the question tag (Act 4 #4 & #6): "Gina hasn\'t been to Angkor Wat, ___?" / "King Sihanouk was born in Phnom Penh, ___?"'),A.c(n5,3,"TG p.184 Act 4: #3 g. don't they?; #7 e. doesn't it?.","g_34_1_4",A.a(["aren't they? / isn't it?","do they? / does it?","didn't they? / wasn't it?",n5],s4),'4. Match the question tag (Act 4 #3 & #7): "Tanya\'s friends believe in the Yeti, ___?" / "The Amazon rainforest crosses 9 countries, ___?"'),A.c(n6,0,"TG p.185 Act 5: #3 were studying; #5 have seen.","g_34_1_5",A.a([n6,"studied / saw","are studying / will seeing","was studying / has seen"],s4),'5. Complete Lina & Tony\'s dialogue (Act 5 #3 & #5): "met while they ___ (study)" and "I wonder if they ___ (see) the monster."'),A.c(n7,1,"TG p.185 Act 5: #7 read (V3); #8 didn't like.","g_34_1_6",A.a(["reading / wasn't like",n7,"readed / don't like","read / hasn't liked"],s4),'6. Complete Act 5 #7 & #8 about Queen Christina of Sweden: "I have just ___ (read) about her. She ___ (not like) wearing the clothes..."'),A.c(n8,2,'TG p.186 Act 6 #1: "ever" in a positive statement should be "never" -> "Kanika has never failed her English exams."',"g_34_1_7",A.a(["Kanika has already fail her English exams.","Kanika have never failed her English exams.",n8,"Kanika is ever failing her English exams."],s4),'7. Correct Activity 6 #1: "Kanika has ever failed her English exams."'),A.c(n9,3,'TG p.186 Act 6 #2 ("I\'ll look") and #6 ("Jin hasn\'t visited ... yet." or "Jin has visited ...").',"g_34_1_8",A.a(["Yes, I'll looking for it. / Jin have visited yet.","Yes, I looked for it right away. / Jin doesn't visited yet.","Yes, I'll look for it. / Jin hasn't already visited yet.",n9],s4),'8. Correct Activity 6 #2 & #6: "Yes, I\'ll looked for it right away." / "Jin has visited her grandparents in the province yet."'),A.c(o0,0,'TG p.186 Act 6 #3: "Tom has already done his cardio exercises. (correct sentence)".',"g_34_1_9",A.a([o0,"The first car was developed by a German invent in 1885.","Roy's decide to eat healthy food only was supported by his family.","Oh, I haven't yet. I'll doing that in a few minutes."],s4),"9. Which sentence in Activity 6 has NO mistakes?"),A.c(o1,1,'SB p.186 Act 8 Example: Indirect questions use statement word order (subject before verb: "glaciers can be").',"g_34_1_10",A.a(["Do you know where did the monarch live?",o1,"Can you tell me what is an era?","Would you mind telling me why does my head ache?"],s4),"10. Choose a grammatically correct indirect question using Activity 8 phrases:")],t1)
l=A.a([A.c(o2,2,'TG p.183 Act 1: "(e.g. civilisation \u2014 tin, salt, civil, ants, sail)".',"v_34_1_1",A.a(["ran, monarch, queen, ship","glacier, bottle, match, torch",o2,"museum, palace, hospital"],s4),'1. In Activity 1 ("Words within words"), which words can ALL be made from the letters of "civilisation"?'),A.c("for a week",3,'SB p.183 Act 3: "You are going to live on an island with two friends for a week."',"v_34_1_2",A.a(["for one day","for a year","for six months","for a week"],s4),"2. In Activity 3, how long will you live on the island with two friends after finding the bottle?"),A.c(o3,0,'SB p.183\u2013184 Act 3: 100-year-old bottle; "We must bring matches. They are useful for making a fire."',"v_34_1_3",A.a([o3,"10 years old; matches are useful for writing notes","50 years old; matches are useful for catching fish","1,000 years old; matches are useful for reading maps"],s4),"3. How old is the bottle in Activity 3, and why do you bring matches?"),A.c(o4,1,'SB p.185 Act 5: "...worked as a search and rescue pilot for the military".',"v_34_1_4",A.a(["a saxophone player",o4,"a film director","a history teacher"],s4),"4. In Activity 5, what did Prince William work as for the military?"),A.c(o5,2,'SB p.185 Act 5: "...met while they were studying at St. Andrews University in Scotland."',"v_34_1_5",A.a(["at Oxford University in England","in Phnom Penh",o5,"in Sweden"],s4),"5. Where did Prince William and Kate meet according to Lina?"),A.c(o6,3,'SB p.185 Act 5: "Well, King Sihanouk directed films, wrote songs and played the saxophone."',"v_34_1_6",A.a(["built gliders, painted portraits, and invented emojis","studied in Scotland, flew rescue planes, and sailed ships","discovered penicillin, wrote papers, and won a Nobel Prize",o6],s4),"6. What three artistic things did Lina say King Sihanouk did?"),A.c(o7,0,'SB p.185 Act 5: She didn\'t like wearing queen clothes or "acting" like a queen.',"v_34_1_7",A.a([o7,"She discovered the Loch Ness monster","She built the Independence Monument in 1958","She won the Nobel Prize for physics"],s4),"7. Why was Queen Christina of Sweden famous according to Tony?"),A.c(o8,1,'TG p.186 Act 6 #4 ("a German inventor") & #5 ("Roy\'s decision").',"v_34_1_8",A.a(["invention & decider",o8,"inventing & deciding","inventor & decided"],s4),'8. In Activity 6 #4 & #5, which two corrected nouns replace "invent" and "decide"?'),A.c(e3,2,"TG p.186 Act 7 #1: monarch (ch = /k/, others = /t\u0283/).","v_34_1_9",A.a(["church","choose","monarch","cheese"],s4),'9. In Activity 7 #1 ("church, choose, cheese, monarch"), which word is pronounced differently?'),A.c(o9,3,"TG p.186 Act 7: #3 headache (/k/); #5 remembered (/d/).","v_34_1_10",A.a(["chocolate (#3) & packed (#5)","chance (#3) & searched (#5)","children (#3) & spent (#5)",o9],s4),'10. In Activity 7 #3 ("headache, chocolate, chance, children") and #5 ("packed, searched, remembered, spent"), which words are odd ones out?')],t1)
l=A.c7("3421","Covers Unit 34 (Book Pages 183\u2013186): Relative pronouns, island modals, question tags, monarchy dialogue tenses, error correction, odd-one-out pronunciation, and indirect questions.",15,t2,"test_unit_34_1",A.a([A.d("p_34_1_1",A.a([e0],s4),"2 syllables: MON-arch (ch = /k/)",e3),A.d("p_34_1_2",A.a([e8],s4),"2 syllables: E-ra (starts with /\u026a\u0259/)","era"),A.d("p_34_1_3",A.a([e8],s4),"2 syllables: HEAD-ache (ch = /k/)",f0),A.d("p_34_1_4",A.a([e0],s4),"3 syllables: BUT-ter-fly (ends in /a\u026a/)",f1),A.d("p_34_1_5",A.a([b],s4),"3 syllables: re-MEM-bered (ends in /d/)",f2)],s6),"Unit 34 \u2014 Test 1",c,b0,l)
t2=A.a([A.c(p0,0,'In an indirect question, the embedded clause uses normal statement word order ("the Royal Palace was built").',"g_34_2_1",A.a([p0,"Do you know when was the Royal Palace built?","Could you tell me when did they build the Royal Palace?","Do you have any idea when was built the Royal Palace?"],s4),'1. Choose the correct indirect question for: "When was the Royal Palace built?"'),A.c(p1,1,'Indirect yes/no questions use "if" or "whether" + subject + auxiliary + verb ("if the rescue pilots have landed").',"g_34_2_2",A.a(["I wonder have the rescue pilots landed safely.",p1,"Can you tell me whether did the rescue pilots land safely?","Do you know if have the rescue pilots landed safely?"],s4),'2. Choose the correct indirect question for the yes/no question: "Have the rescue pilots landed safely?"'),A.c(p2,2,'Life experience ("Have you ever visited"), specific past trip ("went"), and background past action ("while we were studying").',"g_34_2_3",A.a(["visited / have gone / studied","visit / went / are studying",p2,"visiting / was going / studied"],s4),'3. Complete the historical dialogue with the right tenses: "Have you ever _____ (visit) the National Museum?" \u2014 "Yes, I _____ (go) there with my class while we _____ (study) Khmer art last term."'),A.c(p3,3,'"haven\'t run" (negative present perfect) -> "have they?"; "brought" (positive past simple) -> "didn\'t they?".',"g_34_2_4",A.a(["haven't they? / did they?","do they? / wasn't it?","did they? / haven't they?",p3],s4),'4. Complete both question tags: "The campers haven\'t run out of clean water, _____? And they brought a map and a torch, _____?"'),A.c(p4,0,'Use "when" to refer to a time or year ("the historic year").',"g_34_2_5",A.a([p4,"1953 was the historic year who Cambodia gained its independence.","1953 was the historic year which Cambodia gained its independence in that year.","1953 was the historic year where Cambodia gained its independence."],s4),'5. Combine the two sentences using a relative pronoun: "1953 was the historic year. Cambodia gained its independence in that year."'),A.c(p5,1,'Present Perfect ("has already ...") requires the past participle "packed".',"g_34_2_6",A.a(['Change "has" to "did"',p5,'Change "already" to "yet"','Change "Our team" to "They"'],s4),'6. Spot and fix the grammar error: "Our team has already pack the tents, matches, and water bottles for the island trip."'),A.c(p6,2,'After a possessive noun ("Nita\'s") and before "of", we need the noun form "creation".',"g_34_2_7",A.a(['Change "praised" to "praising"','Change "create" to "created"',p6,'Change "camping" to "camped"'],s4),'7. Spot and fix the word-form error: "The teacher praised Nita\'s create of a solar lantern for the camping trip."'),A.c(p7,3,'"just" goes between have/has and V3 in positive sentences; "yet" goes at the end of negative sentences and questions.',"g_34_2_8",A.a(["We have yet eaten lunch, but we haven't packed our bags just.","We didn't eat lunch yet, and we just have pack our bags.","We have already eaten lunch yet, and we just packed.",p7],s4),'8. Which sentence uses "yet" and "just" accurately?'),A.c("mustn't",0,'"mustn\'t" warns strongly against a dangerous action.',"g_34_2_9",A.a(["mustn't","must","have to","should"],s4),'9. Complete the survival sentence with the best modal: "You _____ drink seawater on a desert island because the salt will make you even thirstier."'),A.c("stomach",1,'"stomach" ends in /k/ just like "monarch" and "headache", whereas champion, cherry, and kitchen use /t\u0283/.',"g_34_2_10",A.a(["champion","stomach","cherry","kitchen"],s4),'10. Which word has the SAME /k/ consonant sound for "ch" as "monarch" and "headache"?')],t1)
k=A.a([A.c(e1,2,"A civilisation is an advanced human society with its own culture, cities, and government.","v_34_2_1",A.a(["saxophone","headache","civilisation","match"],s4),'1. Complete the sentence: "Ancient Angkor was a remarkable _____ famous for its stone temples, canals, and reservoirs."'),A.c(e2,3,"A monarchy is a system of government with a king or queen as monarch.","v_34_2_2",A.a(["glacier","decision","promise","monarchy"],s4),'2. Complete the sentence: "Both the United Kingdom and Cambodia have a constitutional _____, where a king or queen is head of state."'),A.c(e4,0,"Search and rescue teams locate and save people who are lost or in danger.","v_34_2_3",A.a([e4,"rock and roll","hide and seek","lost and found"],s4),'3. Complete the sentence: "When two hikers got lost in the mountains during a snowstorm, a _____ helicopter flew out to find them."'),A.c(e7,1,"Glaciers are massive, slow-moving rivers or sheets of ice.","v_34_2_4",A.a(["monarchs","glaciers","saxophones","matches"],s4),'4. Complete the sentence: "As the climate warms, huge icy _____ in polar regions are melting into the sea."'),A.c(e6,2,"The Independence Monument in Phnom Penh was built in 1958.","v_34_2_5",A.a(["Eiffel Tower","St. Andrews University",e6,"Loch Ness"],s4),'5. Complete the sentence: "In Phnom Penh, the lotus-shaped _____ was built in 1958 to celebrate Cambodia\'s freedom."'),A.c(e9,3,"A decision is a choice you make after thinking carefully.","v_34_2_6",A.a(["monarch","headache","empire","decision"],s4),'6. Complete the sentence: "Moving to a new city was a big _____, so the family discussed it carefully for weeks."'),A.c("era",0,"An era is a long and important period of history.","v_34_2_7",A.a(["era","match","headache","pocket"],s4),'7. Complete the sentence: "The Angkorian _____ lasted for several centuries and left behind magnificent temples across Southeast Asia."'),A.c(e5,1,"A saxophone is a brass wind instrument often used in jazz and popular music.","v_34_2_8",A.a(["glacier","saxophone","compass","bottle"],s4),'8. Complete the sentence: "At the jazz concert, the musician played a smooth melody on his shiny brass _____."'),A.c("promise",2,"A promise is a firm statement that you will definitely do something.","v_34_2_9",A.a(["monarch","glacier","promise","legend"],s4),'9. Complete the sentence: "If you make a _____ to help your friend study for the history test, you should keep your word."'),A.c("travelled",3,'"travelled" ends in the voiced /l/ sound, so -ed is pronounced /d/ (unlike washed, laughed, helped which end in /t/).',"v_34_2_10",A.a(["washed","laughed","helped","travelled"],s4),'10. Which past simple verb has a voiced /d/ ending like "remembered" (and NOT a /t/ ending like "packed" or "searched")?')],t1)
