t2=A.a([A.c(p8,0,'SB p.187 Act 2 Example: "Subject Questions: Who went to the beach with friends last weekend?"',"g_35_1_1",A.a([p8,"What do you love?","Where did you go last weekend?","When did you go to the beach?"],s4),'1. From Activity 2 ("I love swimming and I went to the beach with my friends last weekend."), which is the SUBJECT question?'),A.c(p9,1,'TG p.187 Act 3A: 1. arranged; 2. got; 3. feel ("usually" present habit); 4. felt (past trip).',"g_35_1_2",A.a(["arranges / gets / felt / feel",p9,"arranged / get / feeling / felt","arrange / got / feels / felt"],s4),'2. Complete Paul\'s story (Act 3A #1\u20134): "Last September, my school ___ (arrange) some exchange programs and I ___ (get) the chance... I usually ___ (feel) nervous, but I only ___ (feel) excited."'),A.c(q0,2,'TG p.187 Act 3A: 7. stay; 8. visit (general rule); 9. stayed ("this time" past trip).',"g_35_1_3",A.a(["stayed / visited / stay","stay / visited / stays",q0,"staying / visit / stayed"],s4),'3. Complete Act 3A #7\u20139: "For every exchange program, students ___ (stay) with a host family of the country they ___ (visit). Therefore, this time I ___ (stay)..."'),A.c(q1,3,"TG p.187 Act 3A: 13. is; 14. took; 17. had; 18. learnt.","g_35_1_4",A.a(["was / take / have / learn","is / takes / had / learning","were / took / has / learnt",q1],s4),'4. Complete Act 3A #13\u201314 & #17\u201318: "Pchum Ben ___ (be) a national celebration... my host family ___ (take) me to pagoda... I really ___ (have) a great time and ___ (learn) many things."'),A.c(q2,0,'TG p.188 Act 4 #2: "I\'ll lend you some money."',"g_35_1_5",A.a([q2,"I lent you some money yesterday.","I'll buying you a book.","I won't read books."],s4),'5. Give an immediate response using "will" (Act 4 #2): "I need to buy a book, but it\'s so expensive."'),A.c(q3,1,'TG p.189 Act 5 Suggested answers: "Iceland is smaller than Greenland." / "Singapore has the largest population."',"g_35_1_6",A.a(["Singapore is larger than Iceland, and Greenland is the hottest.",q3,"Greenland is the smallest country, and Iceland is hotter than Singapore.","Iceland is more cold than Greenland in winter."],s4),"6. Choose the accurate comparative and superlative sentences from Activity 5:"),A.c(q4,2,'TG p.190 Act 7 #2: "The Colosseum in Italy is visited by over 4 million tourists every year."',"g_35_1_7",A.a(["The Colosseum in Italy was visited by over 4 million tourists every year.","Over 4 million tourists are visited the Colosseum every year.",q4,"The Colosseum in Italy visiting by over 4 million tourists."],s4),'7. Rewrite in PRESENT passive (Act 7 #2): "Over 4 million tourists visit the Colosseum in Italy every year."'),A.c(q5,3,'TG p.190 Act 7 #3: "The Eiffel Tower in Paris was named after Gustave Eiffel."',"g_35_1_8",A.a(["The Eiffel Tower in Paris is named after Gustave Eiffel.","Gustave Eiffel was named after the Eiffel Tower.","The Eiffel Tower in Paris named by them.",q5],s4),'8. Rewrite in PAST passive (Act 7 #3): "They named the Eiffel Tower in Paris after Gustave Eiffel."'),A.c(q6,0,'TG p.190 Act 7 #7: "The first ever mobile phone call was made by Martin Cooper in 1973 in New York City to his rival."',"g_35_1_9",A.a([q6,"The first ever mobile phone call is made by Martin Cooper in 1973.","Martin Cooper was made the first ever mobile phone call in 1973.","The first ever mobile phone call were made in 1973."],s4),'9. Rewrite in PAST passive (Act 7 #7): "Martin Cooper made the first ever mobile phone call in 1973 in New York City to his rival."'),A.c(q7,1,"SB p.190 Act 8 Example: teaches -> taught; is struggling -> was struggling.","g_35_1_10",A.a(["Mrs. Dany said she teaches English to 5 grade 11 classes and is struggling.",q7,"Mrs. Dany said she teaching English and was struggle.","Mrs. Dany told me she will teach 5 grade 11 classes."],s4),'10. Report Mrs. Dany\'s notes (Act 8 Example): "Mrs. Dany: teaches English to 5 different 11 grade classes. Is struggling to find extra resources..."')],t1)
