t2=A.a([A.c(r5,0,'"usually" signals a Present Simple tradition ("prepare"); "last autumn" signals a finished Past Simple event ("taught").',"g_35_2_1",A.a([r5,"prepared / teaches","prepares / taught","are preparing / teach"],s4),'1. Complete the paragraph with Present Simple or Past Simple: "Cambodian families usually _____ (prepare) special rice cakes for Pchum Ben, and last autumn my cousin _____ (teach) me how to wrap them in banana leaves."'),A.c(r6,1,'Spontaneous offers made at the moment of speaking use "I\'ll + base verb".',"g_35_2_2",A.a(["I shared my umbrella with you yesterday.",r6,"I am sharing my umbrella every week.","I'll shared my umbrella with you."],s4),'2. Your friend says: "Oh no, I left my umbrella at home and it\'s starting to rain!" Choose the best immediate offer:'),A.c(r7,2,"400 km\xb2 is the smallest area, and 4 million people is the largest population (most crowded).","g_35_2_3",A.a(["City A has the largest land area, and City B is smaller than City C.","City C is more crowded than City A, and City B is the smallest.",r7,"City B has a larger population than City A."],s4),"3. Compare the three cities using the data: City A (400 km\xb2, 4M people), City B (1,200 km\xb2, 1.5M people), City C (900 km\xb2, 800k people). Which statement is TRUE?"),A.c(r8,3,'"Changi Airport" is singular and "every month" is present simple -> "is used".',"g_35_2_4",A.a(["Changi Airport in Singapore was used by millions of travellers every month.","Changi Airport in Singapore are used by millions of travellers every month.","Millions of travellers are used by Changi Airport every month.",r8],s4),'4. Choose the correct PRESENT passive rewrite: "Millions of travellers use Changi Airport in Singapore every month."'),A.c(r9,0,'Plural subject ("The stone bas-reliefs") + past time ("centuries ago") -> "were carved".',"g_35_2_5",A.a([r9,"The stone bas-reliefs at Angkor Wat was carved by Cambodian artisans centuries ago.","The stone bas-reliefs at Angkor Wat are carved by Cambodian artisans centuries ago.","Cambodian artisans were carved by the stone bas-reliefs centuries ago."],s4),'5. Choose the correct PAST passive rewrite: "Cambodian artisans carved the stone bas-reliefs at Angkor Wat centuries ago."'),A.c(s0,1,"In reported speech: enjoys -> enjoyed; is planning -> was planning.","g_35_2_6",A.a(["Vicheka said that he enjoys speaking English and is planning a cultural club.",s0,"Vicheka told that he enjoying speaking English and was plan a cultural club.","Vicheka said that I enjoyed speaking English and was planning a cultural club."],s4),'6. Report Vicheka\'s interview notes: "Vicheka: enjoys speaking English with exchange students. Is planning a cultural club at school."'),A.c(s1,2,'"Who cooked...?" asks for the subject; "What did your host mother cook...?" asks for the object.',"g_35_2_7",A.a(["Subject Q: What did your host mother cook? | Object Q: Who cooked fish amok?","Subject Q: Who did cook fish amok? | Object Q: What cooked your host mother?",s1,"Subject Q: Where did she cook fish amok? | Object Q: When did she cook it?"],s4),'7. For the sentence "My host mother cooked fish amok for our welcome dinner.", which option pairs the correct SUBJECT question and OBJECT question?'),A.c("should",3,'"should + base verb" gives cultural advice about appropriate behaviour.',"g_35_2_8",A.a(["mustn't","shouldn't","can't","should"],s4),'8. Complete the cultural advice sentence: "When visiting a Buddhist pagoda, you _____ wear respectful clothes that cover your shoulders and knees."'),A.c(s2,0,'Uncountable "coffee" takes singular present passive "is grown", and comparing two countries takes "warmer".',"g_35_2_9",A.a([s2,"was grow / warmest","are grown / more warm","grows / warmest"],s4),'9. Complete the passive comparison: "More coffee _____ in Brazil than in Iceland because Brazil\'s climate is much _____."'),A.c(s3,1,"don't want -> didn't want; my -> his; is -> was; me -> him.","g_35_2_10",A.a(["He said that he doesn't want to leave Cambodia because his host family was kind.",s3,"He said that I didn't want to leave Cambodia because my host family was kind.","He told that he wasn't want to leave Cambodia."],s4),"10. Report the exchange student's sentence: \"I don't want to leave Cambodia because my host family is so kind to me.\"")],t1)
