o=A.a([A.c(b0,1,'"refreshing" (Unit 7A) describes something that makes you feel cool, clean, and full of energy.',"v_7_2_1",A.a(["explosive","refreshing","heavy","scary"],g9),"1. After swimming in the salty sea under the hot sun, drinking cool coconut water felt wonderfully _______."),A.c(a6,0,'A "volcano" (Unit 7A) is a mountain that can erupt with lava, ash, and steam.',"v_7_2_2",A.a(["volcano","waterfall","pond","meadow"],g9),"2. Scientists warned nearby villages when the sleeping _______ began sending ash and steam high into the sky."),A.c(b1,2,'"freshwater" (Unit 7A) is water without salt, unlike ocean water.',"v_7_2_3",A.a(["solar energy","precipitation","freshwater","sand"],g9),"3. Because melting polar ice is mostly _______ rather than salty seawater, Antarctica holds a huge share of the world's drinking-water reserves."),A.c(a7,3,'A "waterfall" (Unit 7A) occurs where a river falls steeply over rocks.',"v_7_2_4",A.a(["desert","hill","island","waterfall"],g9),"4. We hiked along a cool, shaded forest path until we heard the loud roar of a thirty-metre _______ dropping into a rocky pool."),A.c(b2,0,'"solar energy" (Unit 7A) is clean electricity or heat produced from sunlight.',"v_7_2_5",A.a(["solar energy","freshwater","precipitation","lava"],g9),"5. Because desert regions receive intense sunlight almost every day, engineers build huge panels there to collect _______."),A.c(c1,1,'"fluffy" (Unit 7B) means covered with soft, thick fur or feathers.',"v_7_2_6",A.a(["heavy","fluffy","salty","explosive"],g9),"6. Although the small orange kitten looked soft and _______, its claws were surprisingly sharp."),A.c("heavy",2,'"heavy" (Unit 7B) means having great weight and being difficult to lift.',"v_7_2_7",A.a(["light","quick","heavy","adorable"],g9),"7. Lifting the stone box required two strong workers because it was much too _______ for one person."),A.c(b7,3,'A "grizzly bear" (brown bear, Unit 7B) catches fish such as salmon and protects its cubs.',"v_7_2_8",A.a(["scorpion","hamster","cheetah","grizzly bear"],g9),"8. A baby _______ has spots at first and stays close to its mother until it learns how to catch salmon in the river."),A.c("hamster",0,'A "hamster" (Unit 7B) is a tiny furry rodent kept as a pet.',"v_7_2_9",A.a(["hamster","alligator","polar bear","elephant"],g9),"9. Unlike the huge hippopotamus, a pet _______ weighs only a few hundred grams and fits in the palm of your hand."),A.c(b5,1,'A "scorpion" (Unit 7B) is a small desert creature with a curved stinging tail.',"v_7_2_10",A.a(["rabbit","scorpion","penguin","seal"],g9),"10. Hikers must check inside their boots in the morning so a hiding _______ does not sting their toes.")],h6)
