h7=A.a([A.c(g3,0,'Singular subject "a green tree frog" + main verb "live" uses "Does ... live?" and short answer "Yes, it does."',"g_8_2_1",A.a([g3,"Does a green tree frog lives near ponds? Yes, it does.","Is a green tree frog live near ponds? Yes, it is.","Do a green tree frog live near ponds? Yes, it do."],g9),"1. Choose the Yes/No question and short answer that are 100% grammatically CORRECT:"),A.c(g4,1,'Questions asking about ability start with "Can", and plural "tortoises" takes pronoun "they" ("No, they can\'t.").',"g_8_2_2",A.a(["Do / they can't",g4,"Are / they aren't","Can / it can't"],g9),'2. "_______ tortoises swim as fast as sea turtles?" \u2014 "No, _______. Sea turtles have flippers."'),A.c("they aren't",2,'Questions starting with "Are + plural noun" take pronoun short answer "No, they aren\'t."',"g_8_2_3",A.a(["they don't","it isn't","they aren't","snakes aren't"],g9),'3. "Are all snakes dangerous to humans?" \u2014 "No, _______. Most garden snakes are completely harmless."'),A.c("Did / he",2,'"yesterday" + main verb "show" requires "Did", matched by "Yes, he/she did."',"g_8_2_4",A.a(["Does / he","Was / she","Did / he","Is / she"],g9),'4. "_______ your science teacher show a life-cycle diagram in class yesterday?" \u2014 "Yes, _______ did."'),A.c(g1,1,'Uncountable singular subject "liquid pond water" takes "turns into" (never "becomes into").',"g_8_2_5",A.a(["becomes into","turns into","change into","turn into"],g9),'5. Which verb phrase completes the sentence ACCURATELY: "During winter, liquid pond water _______ solid ice."'),A.c(d7,2,'Plural subject "buds" takes the plural verb "change into".',"g_8_2_6",A.a(["changes into","becomes","change into","turns into"],g9),"6. Over several sunny weeks, tiny green flower buds _______ bright red blossoms on the tree."),A.c(g5,0,'Processes begin with "First", move through middle stages with "Next" / "After that", and conclude with "Finally".',"g_8_2_7",A.a([g5,"Finally / First / Then / Next","First / Finally / Next / After that","Next / After that / First / Finally"],g9),'7. Complete the 4-stage rain cycle: "_______, sunlight warms ocean water. _______, the vapour rises and cools. _______, clouds form. _______, rain falls back to the land."'),A.c(g6,0,'"become" is followed directly by a noun ("becomes a pupa"), without the preposition "into".',"g_8_2_8",A.a([g6,'Change "larva" to "larvas"','Change "its" to "their"',"No error"],g9),'8. Spot and fix the grammar error: "The young moth larva becomes into a pupa inside its silk cocoon."'),A.c("it doesn't",2,'Questions starting with "Does + singular noun" take the short answer "No, it doesn\'t."',"g_8_2_9",A.a(["they don't","it isn't","it doesn't","it hasn't"],g9),'9. "Does a gecko have eyelids to blink its eyes?" \u2014 "No, _______. It licks its eyes to keep them clean!"'),A.c(g7,0,'Plural subject "mosquitoes" + base verb "bite" uses "do", and the explanation is grammatically sound.',"g_8_2_10",A.a([g7,"Are butterflies have six legs? Yes, they do.","After that, the baby frog becomes an adult frog finally.","Do a crocodile sleep with one eye open?"],g9),"10. Choose the animal question and explanation that are 100% grammatically CORRECT:")],h6)
